DESCRIPTION:Come to the Responsible AI Community Engagement Project (RAICEP
 ) event in DRA 116!<br><br>This session is titled <b>Responsible AI in Act
 ion: <i>Explore\, Build\, Discuss &amp\; Experience</i></b> and will incl
 ude a mix of discussion and hands-on activities around AI.<br><br>Particip
 ants will explore:<ul><li>The biggest benefits and opportunities associate
 d with AI</li><li>What people need in order to trust AI</li><li>Key trust 
 issues and concerns\, and how these could be addressed</li><li>A hands-on 
 VR experience</li><li>Continued AI agent building and testing</li></ul><br
 >There will also be <strong><b><u>FREE</u></b></strong> food provided at t
 he event for participants! <br><br>For participants looking for something
  more technical\, there will also be an <b>optional advanced activity</b>
  for those who want to go a little deeper and push their AI skills furthe
 r.<br><br>This event is hosted by one of the DATA club's partners: Mark Mc
  Kenzie!
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:Come to the Responsible AI Community Engagemen
 t Project (RAICEP) event in DRA 116!<br><br>This session is titled <b>Resp
